conds since the message was stored."}}},"TrafficOutcome":{"title":"TrafficOutcome","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["code"],"description":"Why a frame was refused or failed.","properties":{"code":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The stable error code the mediator returned to the sender (a trust-task-error or problem-report code).","maxLength":256},"detail":{"type":"string","description":"Short human-readable explanation. Not machine-parsed.","maxLength":1024}}},"WireProtocol":{"title":"WireProtocol","type":"string","enum":["didcomm","didcommV1","tsp","other"],"description":"The protocol a message travelled in, as the mediator detected it from the wire form. `didcomm` is DIDComm v2 (JWE/JWS); `didcommV1` is a DIDComm v1 envelope; `tsp` is a Trust Spanning Protocol message; `other` is anything the mediator could not classify."},"TrafficChannel":{"title":"TrafficChannel","type":"string","enum":["websocket","rest","peerMediator","internal"],"description":"How the traffic reached or left the mediator. `peerMediator` is mediator-to-mediator forwarding."},"TrafficStage":{"title":"TrafficStage","type":"string","enum":["received","stored","delivered","forwarded","refused","deleted","expired","purged"],"description":"What happened. `received`: a frame arrived. `stored`: it was queued for a local account. `delivered`: handed to its recipient. `forwarded`: relayed to another mediator. `refused`: rejected (see the event\'s `outcome`). `deleted`: removed by its recipient or an administrator. `expired`: removed by expiry. `purged`: removed by a queue purge."},"TrafficDirection":{"title":"TrafficDirection","type":"string","enum":["inbound","outbound","internal"],"description":"`inbound`: arriving at the mediator. `outbound`: leaving it (delivery to a recipient, or a forward to another mediator). `internal`: a state change with no wire traffic (expiry, deletion, purge)."}}}';

